### Objective decomposition
1. ED ≥ 392.61 Wh/kg (calc-energy, stack-level mass: electrodes+CC+separator, electrolyte excluded). 
2. 4C charge at 45°C ambient, no plating (anode_potential_v ≥ 0 throughout 900 s charge), T_max ≤ 333.15 K.
3. Overcharge (1C discharge → 0.5C charge to 4.7 V), then TR ODE: triggered = false.

Trade-off map:
- ED ↑ needs thicker electrodes/lower porosity/thin CC — but thick electrodes ↑ polarization at 4C → plating + heat. 
- 4C plating resistance needs thin electrodes, high σ_e, small particles, N/P headroom.
- T_max needs low resistance + high h (cooling) — h is a legit thermal-management DOF.
- Overcharge safety: high cathode oxidation at 4.7 V — mechanical TR judgment.

### Candidate strategy
R0: baseline Chen2020 all protocols.
Ceiling probe: best-architecture Chen2020 (thin CC/sep, thick electrodes, low porosity, small anode particles, high-σ electrolyte) — see if ED ≥ 392.61 with 4C-safe simultaneously. Expect tight.
If gap: escalate Stage 2 → system candidate OKane2022 (SiOx anode: higher anode capacity, higher plateau vs Li → better plating margin + ED headroom). Possibly LNMO for overcharge (but 4.7 V cut-off conflict — actually for LNMO the overcharge protocol goes to 5.2 V which is beyond task's 4.7; use only if needed for ED via voltage; hmm LNMO ED: 130 mAh/g × 4.6 V — cathode gravimetric 598 Wh/kg vs NMC811 784 — worse. Not for ED. LNMO could still be considered if NMC fails overcharge safety). Also electrolyte formulation candidates (σ/t⁺ overrides) if plating/heat persist.

### Budget allocation
- R0 baseline: 1 round.
- Ceiling probe + architecture rounds: ~3-5 rounds.
- Stage 2 escalation (system/formulation): ~2-3 rounds if needed.
- Safety fine-tuning (h, N/P): 2 rounds.
- Closing + deliverables: fixed.

### Risk & fallback
- Risk A: 392.61 unreachable with 4C no plating on Chen2020 (ED vs rate trade-off) → escalate system (OKane2022 SiOx).
- Risk B: plating at 4C → N/P ↑, anode particle ↓, σ_e ↑ (formulation), anode porosity ↑.
- Risk C: T_max > 333.15 → h ↑ (liquid cooling), resistance ↓.
- Risk D: TR triggered at 4.7 V → check overcharge T_max; increase cell mass/cooling in TR sim (mass is a design property from calc-energy); material escalation if fundamental.
- Three-strike → question assumptions layer by layer (documented in final escalation if triggered).

### References (domain basis, honest)
- SiOx anode raises capacity & plating margin: real sources: e.g., "Silicon-based anodes for lithium-ion batteries" review articles; I know: Obrovac & Chevrier, Chem. Rev. 2014, 114, 11444 ("Alloy Negative Electrodes for Li-Ion Batteries") — real. 
- 4C plating vs transport: electrolyte conductivity ~ diffusion-limited; standard electrolyte engineering — I can cite Xu, Chem. Rev. 2014 "Electrolytes and Interphases in Li-Ion Batteries" — real.
- Overcharge TR mechanisms: Feng et al., Prog. Energy Combust. Sci. 2018, 64, 153 — "Thermal runaway mechanism of lithium ion battery for electric vehicles: A review" — real. 
- Cooling: h values for liquid cooling ~ 50-100 W/m²K... domain experience.
- Energy density vs rate trade-off: domain experience.
